From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:59:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: Do not lose an unplug reported while resuming

dcpep_cb_hotplug() decides under hotplug_lock that a report is ignored
because the DCP is suspended, but marks the mode invalid and the
hotplug work pending only after dropping the lock. dcp_hpd_resume()
clears suspended under the lock and reads hotplug_pending after
dropping it. If the resume runs between the two, it sees no pending
work, and the report then leaves the mode invalid with nothing to send
a hotplug event or set the link status: the display stays black until
it is replugged. Commit e735f09411dd ("drm: apple: Invalidate the mode
on an unplug reported while suspended") describes j473 reporting such
an unplug right around the end of resume.

Mark the mode invalid and the work pending inside the locked section,
and have dcp_hpd_resume() read hotplug_pending in the section that
clears suspended. A report is then either ignored and seen by the
resume, or handled normally.

Fixes: e735f09411dd ("drm: apple: Invalidate the mode on an unplug reported while suspended")
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqitcmCNS6G33aQUShi39x
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c            |  8 +++++++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c | 11 ++++++-----
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index a69cfc8..3d74ec6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -836,18 +836,24 @@ void dcp_hpd_suspend(struct platform_device *pdev)
 void dcp_hpd_resume(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct apple_dcp *dcp = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
+	bool pending;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dcp->power_mutex);
 	WRITE_ONCE(dcp->stopping, false);
 	mutex_unlock(&dcp->power_mutex);
+	/*
+	 * A report ignored while suspended sets hotplug_pending under the
+	 * same lock, so it is either seen here or not ignored at all.
+	 */
 	spin_lock(&dcp->hotplug_lock);
 	dcp->suspended = false;
+	pending = dcp->hotplug_pending;
 	spin_unlock(&dcp->hotplug_lock);
 	if (dcp->hdmi_hpd_irq)
 		enable_irq(dcp->hdmi_hpd_irq);
 	if (dcp->hdmi_hpd)
 		schedule_work(&dcp->hpd_resume_wq);
-	if (dcp->connector && READ_ONCE(dcp->hotplug_pending))
+	if (dcp->connector && pending)
 		schedule_work(&dcp->connector->hotplug_wq);
 }
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
index faca88a..81601d8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_template.c
@@ -1101,19 +1101,20 @@ static void dcpep_cb_hotplug(struct apple_dcp *dcp, u64 *connected)
 	spin_lock(&dcp->hotplug_lock);
 	ignored = dcp->suspended;
 	deferred = !ignored && dcp->during_modeset;
-	if (ignored && !*connected)
+	if (ignored && !*connected) {
 		dcp->hotplug_seq++;
+		dcp->valid_mode = false;
+		/* seen by dcp_hpd_resume() once it clears suspended */
+		WRITE_ONCE(dcp->hotplug_pending, true);
+	}
 	if (deferred) {
 		dcp->hotplug_deferred = true;
 		dcp->hotplug_deferred_connected = !!*connected;
 	}
 	spin_unlock(&dcp->hotplug_lock);
 
-	if (ignored && !*connected) {
-		dcp->valid_mode = false;
-		WRITE_ONCE(dcp->hotplug_pending, true);
+	if (ignored && !*connected)
 		schedule_work(&dcp->vblank_wq);
-	}
 
 	if (!deferred && !ignored)
 		dcp_apply_hotplug(dcp, !!*connected);
